lisa-design:
- Risk score is sourced from the CURRENT risk row (risk_register_risks.likelihood x impact via riskrel.NumericalRiskScore, 1-25) plus risk_register_risks.status, NOT from risk_scores snapshots. Simpler than a latest-score CTE and matches the "likelihood x impact 1-25" spec. Buckets: open/investigating/mitigating-planned -> openScoreSum (heat); risk-accepted/mitigating-implemented -> mutedScoreSum; remediated/closed excluded. Deduped by risk id per node.
- Closure direction: control_links store concrete->abstract (source implements/documents target). The lineage tree renders abstract->concrete, so children/closure walk edges in REVERSE (target -> its sources). ControlLinkGraph.EvidenceClosure follows `implements` edges only (the evidence/risk math path, includes the node itself); StructuralClosure additionally follows `documents` (structure + linkage counts only). `documents` is presence-only, excluded from compliance/risk sums, per the vocabulary matrix.
- Cycle prevention uses the mathematically-correct check (WouldCreateCycle: does target already reach source over ALL edge types, or is it a self-loop) rather than the spec's looser "target in source's downstream closure" phrasing. This guarantees the combined graph stays a DAG. Walks are visited-set guarded so pre-existing cycles are tolerated everywhere.
- catalog_type is the CANONICAL column (never derived from link presence -> rootness). OSCAL round-trip rides a metadata prop {name:catalog-type, ns:https://compliance-framework.github.io/ns}. Standard catalogs OMIT the prop so pre-existing catalogs round-trip byte-identically. UnmarshalOscal (and thus the import path) reads it straight back; import needed no change.
- GetEvidenceStatusCountsByFilters (service/relational/evidence.go) keeps the batch map signature but internally loops one query per filter (PoC corner). profile_compliance.go was deliberately NOT refactored onto it, to keep blast radius small. Per-control status merges its filters' counts then applies computeLineageStatus (identical semantics to profile compliance: any not-satisfied wins, else satisfied, else unknown).
- Scoping: sspId restricts STANDARD controls to the SSP's resolved profile controls (ssp_profiles -> profile_controls, control id folded via UPPER); policy/procedure controls are always in scope but their metrics are SSP-scoped. Filters use `ssp_id IS NULL OR ssp_id = ?`; risks use risk.ssp_id. componentId scoping IS implemented (evidence via evidence_components EXISTS on l.id; risks via risk_component_links) rather than deferred.
- control_links has a composite PK (source cat+ctrl, target cat+ctrl, relationship_type) and NO DB-level FK constraints (PoC corner). Endpoint existence is validated app-side in the handler (resolveControlType). control_links.control_catalog columns are uuid+text, matching risk_control_links (NOT filter_controls' text-catalog-id gotcha).
- Node keys: `catalog:<uuid>`, `group:<catId>/<groupId>`, `control:<catId>/<controlId>`. Group nesting is flattened to top-level groups for the children view; a group node's rollup still covers its full (nested) control subtree. An anchored policy control appears both under the standard control it implements and under its own policy-catalog root with the SAME key and metrics (one DAG node rendered twice) - this is intentional.
- authz: added `control-link:[read,create,delete]` and `lineage:[read]` resources to manifest.yaml + authz constants, and granted them to the contributor role (admin/viewer covered by their `*` wildcards; auditor `*:[read]` covers reads). Routes guarded with pep.For(ResourceControlLink)/pep.For(ResourceLineage).
